From 2e6fa1dd2e55de2997fe137ac700590ffefe50d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 06:59:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 31/41] [TSReader] Give audio without a PTS the clock of the
 next PTS

The clock of an audio stream that starts with PES packets without a PTS
comes from the next PTS less the durations of the frames before. The read
ahead in the segment could not find a PTS in the next segment, so a short
segment without a PTS came without PTS values. A seek scan started with
parsers without a clock, so a seek could not land on a frame before the
first PTS of the segment. A resume position of 0, the start of the
stream, also had no clock.

The sample reader now holds the audio frames before the first PTS of the
stream, up to 1 s (a stream needs a PTS every 0.7 s), and gives them the
clock of that PTS. Other streams do not wait. At the end of the stream, or
after 1 s, the frames come without a PTS. A live wait keeps them. A seek
drops them. This replaces the read ahead at the start.

A seek scan after a reset of the parsers first finds the clocks at the
scan start, so the scan has the PTS of each frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
